"""Render measured groups, per-root comparison and explicitly bounded latent evidence."""
import collections,json
from pathlib import Path
out=Path(__file__).resolve().parent
read=lambda n:json.loads((out/n).read_text())
p=read('provenance.json');groups=read('grouped-first-stops.json');art=read('root-order.json');totals=read('latent-totals.json');entry=totals['guarded_entry'];ordinary=totals['ordinary_counted_observations']
checks={r['root']:r for r in art['checks']};excerpts=read('source-excerpts.json');comparison=read('comparison.json')
accepted=[root for g in groups if g['kind']=='accepted' for root in g['roots']]
q=lambda s:'`'+str(s)+'`'
lines=['# Next stops on main b322b6ba','','Measured for #baobab and #b5w3ycg. Report only.','',f'Compiler and apply SHA: {q(p["sha"])}. TypeScript 6.0.3 source pin: {q(p["typescript_pin"])}.','',f'Box: {q(p["box"])}; {p["cpus"]} visible CPUs; CPU quota {q(p["cpu_max"])}; {p["meminfo"]}. Started {p["date"]}.','','## Grouped first stops','','Locations and root names are relative to `src/compiler/`. Sorted largest first. Only the first of each root\'s two observations counts. All duplicate observations agree in every non-timing field.','','| Roots | Location | Kind | Exact reason | Compared with c3b7baf0 | Root names |','| ---: | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |']
for g in groups:
 names=', '.join(q(r)+(' ('+checks[r]['classification']+')' if r in checks else '') for r in g['roots'])
 reason=g['reason'].replace('|','\\|')
 lines.append(f'| {g["count"]} | {q(g["where"])} | {g["kind"]} | {reason} | {g["comparison"]} | {names} |')
lines+=['','## Roots lowering whole','',f'{len(accepted)}/79 in the ordinary independent-root census: '+', '.join(map(q,accepted))+'.','','This measures Lower acceptance of each complete resolved root program. Native output is not measured. Readiness roots receive no additional acceptance credit.','','## Comparison with c3b7baf0','','Baseline compiler/apply SHA: `c3b7baf0b3438bf5ac7aa9fcf6eb2ba385e2f9bd`, from `typescript/next-stops-c3b7baf0`. Its report and grouped table are retained in `previous-REPORT.md` and `previous-grouped-first-stops.json`.','','Unchanged means the same location, kind and exact reason for that root. Moved means a different tuple already present in the baseline. New means a tuple absent from the baseline.','','| Current group | Roots | Unchanged roots | Moved roots | New roots |','| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |']
for g in groups:
 c=collections.Counter(r['classification'] for r in comparison if r['root'] in g['roots'])
 lines.append(f'| {q(g["where"])} {g["kind"]} | {g["count"]} | {c["unchanged"]} | {c["moved"]} | {c["new"]} |')
lines+=['','Each root, with its before and after tuple retained in `comparison.json`:','','| Root | Classification | Before location / kind | After location / kind |','| --- | --- | --- | --- |']
for r in comparison:lines.append(f'| {q(r["root"])} | {r["classification"]} | {q(r["before"][0])} {r["before"][1]} | {q(r["after"][0])} {r["after"][1]} |')
lines+=['','## Stop source and lowering emitters','']
emitters={'an ambient value declaration':'`internal/lower/ambient.go:79` assigns the exact reason in `ambientRefusal`; line 91 emits the `Refused` result.','a cast the runtime can\'t check':'`internal/lower/cast_proof.go:195`, `castRefusal`.','reading an enum before its runtime initialization; move the call after the enum declaration':'`internal/lower/namespaces.go:267` and `:318`, `namespaceInitialization`.','a namespace read before runtime initialization, directly or through a reachable call; move that read or call after the namespace declaration':'`internal/lower/namespaces.go:269` and `:321`, `namespaceInitialization`.'}
for g in groups:
 if g['where']=='-':continue
 assert g['reason'] in emitters,g
 e=next(e for e in excerpts if e['where']==g['where'])
 lines += [f'### {g["where"]} ({g["comparison"]})','',f'{g["kind"]}: {q(g["reason"])}. '+emitters[g['reason']],'',f'Source lines {e["start_line"]} through {e["end_line"]}:','','```ts',e['text'].rstrip(),'```','']
lines+=['## Root-order classification','','The same `stage3/meter/report.py` criteria and `node_readiness.py` helper as the baseline are used. Classification requires entry attempted-source and readiness-finding evidence, plus a Node throw. The ordinary first stops remain counted above.','',f'Entry classification: **{art["status"]}**. {art.get("stopping_reason") or "The per-source ledger completed."}','',f'Entry emitted {art["entry_stream_records"]} stream records and completed {art["completed_sources"]}/{art["expected_sources"]} source records.','','| Root | Independent stop | Node exit | First error | Label |','| --- | --- | ---: | --- | --- |']
for r in art['checks']:lines.append(f'| {q(r["root"])} | {q(r["where"])} | {r["node"]["exit"]} | {r["node"]["first_error"]} | {r["classification"]} |')
s=entry['child_status'];c=entry['finding_totals'];o=ordinary['first_stop_totals']
lines+=['','## Latent totals','',f'Guarded entry run, `LATENT_FULL=1`, `LATENT_ASSERT_NO_OUTPUT=1`, bound 1800 seconds: child exit {q(s["exit_code"])}, elapsed {s["seconds"]:.3f} seconds, stopping reason {q(s["stopping_reason"] or "completed")}. Checker diagnostics: {entry["checker_diagnostics"]}.','',f'Emitted guarded-entry findings: **NotYet {c["NotYet"]}, Refused {c["Refused"]}, panics {c["panic"]}**. Completed sources: {entry["completed_sources"]}/{entry["expected_sources"]}.']
if not entry['complete']:lines+=['','The entry run did not finish inside its bound. These counts cover emitted records only. Unemitted findings are unknown; these are not complete-program latent totals. The stream carries no completed source ledger beyond the coverage stated above.']
lines+=['',f'Ordinary census, summed over the 79 counted first observations: **NotYet {o["NotYet"]}, Refused {o["Refused"]}, panics {o["panic"]}**, plus {len(accepted)} accepted. The ordinary stream carries no latent totals. These are first-stop counts only; full latent totals for the ordinary census are unavailable. `latent-totals.py` and `latent-totals.json` retain the calculation and labels.','','## Method, checkpoints and cleanup','','The baseline REPORT.md method and scripts were read before execution. The measurement recipe is reused at b322b6ba: one apply tree, an ordinary binary from the same SHA with no overlay, sorted roots in sequential groups of 20, 20, 20 and 19, two raw observations per root, first observation counted. `group-*.jsonl` contains 158 observations; `census.jsonl` contains the 79 counted observations.','','Setup: `source /workspace/adamic-tools/env.sh`, `bash cloud/setup.sh`, `npm ci --prefix stage3/api`, and `export ADAMIC_TYPESCRIPT_SOURCE=/workspace/scratch/typescript-source`, whose HEAD is the pin above. Setup, dependency installation, apply and both binary builds exited 0.','','Apply: `bash stage3/apply.sh /workspace/scratch/next-stops-adapted`. Ordinary build: `go build -o /workspace/scratch/next-stops-census ./stage3/census/tool`. Guarded build uses the selected SHA\'s `stage3/census/latent/make_overlay.py` and `stage3/meter/entry_overlay.py`, then `go build -overlay=/workspace/scratch/next-stops-entry-overlay/overlay.json -o /workspace/scratch/next-stops-entry ./stage3/census/latent/tool`. The guarded binary cannot emit usable IR.','','`binaries.json`, build information, source manifests, scripts, command/status ledgers and raw streams identify the measured bytes and child exits. Each census process group was killed and reaped after the child exit. `validation.json` verifies 79 roots, 158 observations, duplicate agreement, source cleanliness and no surviving census processes. Anything over 1 MB is gzip-compressed.','','The initial extra preparation checkpoint found the previous run\'s remote checkpoint and was rejected. The existing tip was fetched, then the fresh evidence was appended with a plain fast-forward push. The required apply checkpoint was pushed immediately after apply, followed by a checkpoint after every root group. `checkpoint-*-status.json` records the results.','','An unintended outer preparation-plus-pipeline timeout wrapper was paused while its child continued in the original foreground session, then resumed after pipeline completion to collect the child\'s actual exit code. This did not change root order, root limits, binaries or observations; `pipeline-supervision.json` records the intervention.','','The final branch `typescript/next-stops-b322b6ba` contains one report-only commit directly on b322b6ba. All changes are under this directory. No force-push was used and main was never pushed.']
text='\n'.join(lines)+'\n';assert '\u2014' not in text and '\u2013' not in text
(out/'REPORT.md').write_text(text)
